# Weakens E's StaleEpochNeverAppends and RaisedEpochUnique in this module's
# environment: a superseded activation, whose claim was raised earlier, still has
# its stamped appends allocated. The current activation's claim head does not
# cover them, and its live advance passes one. Shows the assumption is
# load-bearing.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestAssumeSupersededAllocates
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: any activation whose claim was raised allocates, current or superseded
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc
BOUNDS: WithPreArm = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ a \in up
    /\ cur = a
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ a \in up
\* MUTATION: a superseded activation still allocates.
    /\ claimed[a]
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END
